1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:08,400
The corridor didn't end; it looped. With every pass, the walls rendered at lower resolution as the system ran out of memory.

2
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:18,200
Compiling User Abhrankan, forty-one percent. The text no longer printed on the monitors. It burned directly into his retina.

3
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:28,000
He breaks into the Main Distribution Frame. Here, the core Cisco backbone switch is still running on bare metal, untouched by the compiler.

4
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:37,400
Latency spikes to one hundred and fifty milliseconds. He plugs into the serial console as the exit behind him completely vanishes.

5
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:47,000
Sixty-seven percent. His vision drops from true color to harsh eight-bit VGA. The compiler begins overwriting his memories.

6
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:56,600
His left arm locks in a rigid spasm as foreign drivers load into his nerves. With one hand, he writes a hardware access control list.

7
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:06,200
Eighty-nine percent. He binds the firewall and strikes Enter. The fans die. Time freezes to zero milliseconds.

8
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:17,400
Connection reset by peer. The packet is dropped. But the doorway returns misaligned by three inches. The bug in reality remains.

9
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:18,000
SERVER ROOM B — Chapter 3: Link Stage
